{"id": "Dew8pbeR6M8", "title": "Video by practicalskills.ai", "description": "LangChain, LangGraph, LangSmith. Three names, one company, and one mix-up most people carry.\n\nThey aren't rivals. They're three layers of one stack:\n\n\ud83d\udd39 LangChain is the parts: models, prompts, tools\n\ud83d\udd39 LangGraph  is the engine: state, loops, agents\n\ud83d\udd39 LangSmith is the instruments: traces, evals, monitoring\n\nSo \"LangChain or LangGraph?\" is the wrong question. Ask three instead:\n\n1\ufe0f\u20e3 Whose parts?\n2\ufe0f\u20e3 Whose engine?\n3\ufe0f\u20e3 Whose instruments?\n\nYou can pick all three, or mix and match with other tools. Each layer works on its own.\n\nWhich layers are you using right now? Drop your three picks in the comments \ud83d\udc47\n\nHashtags:\n#LangChain #LangGraph #LangSmith #AIAgents #LLM GenAI AIEngineering MachineLearning AIDevelopers AgenticAI LLMOps PromptEngineering TechExplained LearnAI PracticalSkills\n\nI kept the ending as a comments prompt to match the \"Drop it\" card on the last slide, and left out any share, save or follow lines, as you asked.", "channel": "practicalskills.ai", "uploader_id": "79716631700", "uploader": "Practicalskills.ai", "timestamp": 1792603805, "like_count": 118, "comment_count": 3, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1646836893629589a", "manifest_url": null, "ext": "m4a", "width": null, "height": null, "tbr": 53.77, "asr": 48000, "fps": null, "language": null, "format_note": "DASH audio", "filesize": null, "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "dynamic_range": null, "url": "https://scontent-sjc3-1.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNbV6IDuXu5rAm1E